     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><br>Hi all,<div><br></div><div>I&#39;m learning about renderUI / uiOutputs with selectInput(), but haven&#39;t found an example which addresses my question. (I&#39;ll put together a repeatable example this afternoon if requested.)</div><div><br></div><div>So, we have two selectInputs rendered dynamically from server.R, one which accepts multiple selections, the other which is restricted to one. This logic needs to be interchangeable, if you will.</div><div><br></div><div>That is to say, I need to enforce the rule that </div><div> - when uiOutput(&quot;A&quot;) has only one element selected, </div><div> - the uiOutput(&quot;B&quot;) should get &quot;multiple = TRUE&quot; to allow multiple selections.</div><div> - and if the user made multiple selections in uiOutput(&quot;A&quot;) they should be restricted to one in uiOutput(&quot;B&quot;).<br></div><div><br></div><div>Is there already an example of this in the amazing archive of Shiny examples? I&#39;m imagining a reactive() section with an isolate call, but I&#39;m quite lost in the implementation.</div><div><br></div><div>Thanks very much</div><div>Jeff</div></div>"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "z6IlOuDSBQAJ",
   "from": "Sigbert Klinke",
